                {
                  "type": "quiz",
                  "title": "Knowledge Check: Full Patient Scenario",
                  "content": "A patient has a $1,500 annual deductible (not yet met this year) and 20% coinsurance. She receives a covered procedure. The provider bills $4,000; the allowed amount is $3,500. What is the patient's total responsibility for this procedure?\n\nA. $700 (20% of the full $3,500 allowed amount)\nB. $1,500 (just the deductible - coinsurance only starts next visit)\nC. $1,900 ($1,500 deductible + 20% of the remaining $2,000)\nD. $3,500 (full allowed amount because deductible was not met)\n\n---\n\n**Answer: C**\n\n**Explanation:** Work through it step by step. Step 1: Patient pays the first $1,500 of the $3,500 allowed amount to meet the deductible. Remaining = $3,500 - $1,500 = $2,000. Step 2: Coinsurance kicks in on the $2,000 remaining. Patient pays 20% of $2,000 = $400. Plan pays 80% of $2,000 = $1,600. Step 3: Patient total = $1,500 + $400 = $1,900. The provider write-off is $4,000 - $3,500 = $500 (contractual adjustment, not collectible). Answer A is wrong because it skips the deductible and applies coinsurance to everything. Answer B is wrong because coinsurance applies within the same claim once the deductible is met - not just on the next visit.",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"98\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"20\">Full scenario - put it all together</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"130\" width=\"300\" height=\"170\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"175\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"16\">DEDUCTIBLE</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"218\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"28\">$1,500</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"258\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"14\">not yet met</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"288\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"14\">this plan year</text><rect x=\"400\" y=\"130\" width=\"300\" height=\"170\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.12)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"175\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"16\">COINSURANCE</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"218\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"28\">80/20</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"258\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"14\">plan pays 80%</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"288\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"14\">patient pays 20%</text><rect x=\"740\" y=\"130\" width=\"300\" height=\"170\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"890\" y=\"175\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"16\">ALLOWED AMT</text><text x=\"890\" y=\"218\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"28\">$3,500</text><text x=\"890\" y=\"258\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"14\">billed was $4,000</text><text x=\"890\" y=\"288\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"14\">write-off: $500</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"340\" width=\"980\" height=\"110\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.12)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"380\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"18\">Step 1: Patient pays deductible first</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"418\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"17\">Patient pays $1,500 - deductible met. Remaining: $3,500 - $1,500 = $2,000</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"470\" width=\"980\" height=\"110\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"510\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"18\">Step 2: Apply coinsurance to remaining $2,000</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"548\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"17\">Patient: 20% of $2,000 = $400 | Plan: 80% of $2,000 = $1,600</text><rect x=\"60\" y=\"610\" width=\"460\" height=\"100\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.20)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"290\" y=\"652\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"18\">PATIENT TOTAL</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"695\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"26\">$1,900</text><rect x=\"580\" y=\"610\" width=\"460\" height=\"100\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"rgba(59,130,246,0.20)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"810\" y=\"652\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"18\">PLAN PAYS</text><text x=\"810\" y=\"695\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"26\">$1,600</text><text x=\"290\" y=\"730\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"14\">$1,500 deductible + $400 coinsurance</text><text x=\"810\" y=\"730\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"14\">80% of $2,000 remaining</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"810\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">Plus: provider write-off of $500 (billed $4,000 minus allowed $3,500)</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"848\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"16\">That $500 is NOT collectible from the patient (in-network contractual adjustment).</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "Final check - trace every dollar through deductible, coinsurance, and write-off"
                  },
                  "question": "A patient has a $1,500 annual deductible (not yet met this year) and 20% coinsurance. She receives a covered procedure. The provider bills $4,000; the allowed amount is $3,500. What is the patient's total responsibility for this procedure?",
                  "options": [
                    {"text":"$700 (20% of the full $3,500 allowed amount)","correct":false},
                    {"text":"$1,500 (just the deductible - coinsurance only starts next visit)","correct":false},
                    {"text":"$1,900 ($1,500 deductible + 20% of the remaining $2,000)","correct":true},
                    {"text":"$3,500 (full allowed amount because deductible was not met)","correct":false}
                  ],
                  "explanation": "Work through it step by step. Step 1: Patient pays the first $1,500 of the $3,500 allowed amount to meet the deductible. Remaining = $3,500 - $1,500 = $2,000. Step 2: Coinsurance kicks in on the $2,000 remaining. Patient pays 20% of $2,000 = $400. Plan pays 80% of $2,000 = $1,600. Step 3: Patient total = $1,500 + $400 = $1,900. The provider write-off is $4,000 - $3,500 = $500 (contractual adjustment, not collectible). Answer A is wrong because it skips the deductible and applies coinsurance to everything. Answer B is wrong because coinsurance applies within the same claim once the deductible is met - not just on the next visit."
                }
