                  "explanation": "Balance billing is the amount an out-of-network provider charges above what the insurer considers the allowed amount. Because it is an out-of-network charge, it generally does not count toward the in-network OOP max - meaning the patient can be hit with this bill on top of their full OOP max spending. This is why surprise billing protections (like the No Surprises Act for certain situations) matter so much. Always advise patients to confirm network status before receiving care."
